WEBVTT

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.170
Anna asks Claude how the

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:09.480
MRR has developed this year.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.640
She never says which region,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.210
but her login does.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.570
So the answer is 11.9 million.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.950
The MRR for EMEA.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.230
Ben asks exactly the same

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.090
question and gets 15.8 million,

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.550
the number for his region.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.720
David works in two regions, so he sees

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.830
two rows, EMEA and APAC side by side.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:44.930
One definition.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.100
One server.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.190
Your login decides the rows.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.500
Canonic, let your agents

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.430
query your data correctly.
